# Patch files must stay LF on disk.
#
# `git apply` matches an LF working tree. With core.autocrlf=true (set on the
# Windows box this repo is developed on) git checked these .patch files out
# with CRLF, so `git apply --check` failed on EVERY file after `hermes update`
# even though the committed blobs and the working-tree base were unchanged.
# That looks exactly like upstream drift and sends you hand-porting hunks that
# never needed porting. No EOL conversion for patch payloads.
*.patch text eol=lf
